    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0107" n="9" xml:id="pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/212: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva (Gilbert) to the Acting Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-05-10T14:00:00+01:00">May 10, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 10—11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>183. Consulate’s 167, May 3, 11 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">noon?</hi>]<anchor
                        n="8" xml:id="d10-f1"/> The Council (Matos, Guatemala, presiding for this
                    session) this morning received and transmitted to the Assembly the Lytton Report
                    dated April 30:<anchor n="9" xml:id="d10-f2"/> The representative of Japan made
                    an oral reservation maintaining Japan’s position respecting the nonapplicability
                    of article 15.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d10-f3"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center"> . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
